{
	"name": "Google Sheets content calendar to sprkly",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "ec3457c8-0952-4171-be75-a448bf6b24f2",
			"name": "Overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-1000,
				-80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Post from a Google Sheet with sprkly\n\n### How it works\n- Every 15 minutes it reads the rows with Status **Approved**.\n- The sprkly node checks each row: a caption, a time that has not come yet, known accounts and web links for media.\n- A good row becomes a scheduled post. External ID `sheet-<Row ID>` means a re-run never posts twice. A row with no Row ID, or a Row ID used twice, gets **Error**.\n- A bad row gets Status **Error** and a plain reason. The other rows still go.\n- Each row gets back its Status, sprkly Post ID, time, link and error.\n- When a post goes out, the row gets **Published** and the link. When it fails, **Failed** and the reason.\n\n### Setup\n- Needs the community node `n8n-nodes-sprkly` 0.2.0 or later: https://github.com/ahlanlhw/n8n-nodes-sprkly\n- Add your sprkly API key to the 3 sprkly nodes. API docs: https://sprkly.app/docs/api\n- Add your Google login to the 3 sheet nodes, and pick your sheet in each.\n- Columns: Row ID, Status, Caption, Schedule Time, Accounts, Media URL, sprkly Post ID, Scheduled For, Link, Error. Keep Schedule Time as plain text.\n- Give every row its own Row ID. A row without one is never posted.\n- Set your time zone in Workflow settings. Times in the sheet use it.\n\n### Customization\n- Change how often it runs in **Every 15 minutes**.\n- Add a Title column for TikTok and YouTube, and map it in **Schedule post in sprkly**, under Additional Fields.",
				"height": 760,
				"width": 520,
				"color": 1
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "4b65bbe4-ec51-401d-9e26-a4ea89666cf0",
			"name": "Note: schedule rows",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Schedule approved rows\nThe sprkly node checks each row and gives back one result row. An empty Schedule Time is refused, so nothing posts by accident. The result goes back to the same row.",
				"height": 420,
				"width": 1000,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "871dfeb1-048d-4286-8b46-7954b732b905",
			"name": "Note: track posts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				620
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Track what happened\nWhen a post goes out or fails, the row is found by its Row ID. Only posts with an External ID that starts with sheet- reach this sheet. A post with no Row ID is skipped.",
				"height": 440,
				"width": 760,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
